WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.600
Is Moon Knight just Marvel’s version of DC’s&nbsp;
Batman? No! Not at all. What, then, makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.440
them different and distinct? Origin story? Powers?&nbsp;
Intellect? Let’s take a look at all that and more!

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.320
Everyone knows the story of Batman's&nbsp;
family. Bruce Wayne, an only child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.880
grew up as the heir to the billion-dollar Wayne&nbsp;
Enterprises. His parents, Martha and Thomas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.680
were wealthy socialites and philanthropists&nbsp;
dedicated to using their money to improve lives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:30.880
in Gotham City. One night, the Waynes took their&nbsp;
son to a show, but they were accosted by a thug&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.840
in the alley after leaving. The mugging went&nbsp;
awry, and both of Bruce's parents were killed.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.680
Moon Knight's family history could&nbsp;
hardly be more different from Batman's.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:44.000
Young Marc Spector grew up in Chicago&nbsp;
with his father Elias and younger brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.440
Randall. Elias was a rabbi who escaped the&nbsp;
Nazis to make a new life for himself in America.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.400
He encouraged his boys to avoid violence in&nbsp;
any conflict. Elias died when Marc was still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:58.640
a young man, but Marc's brother Randall&nbsp;
remained a big part of his life, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:03.360
eventually became the supervillain Shadowknight,&nbsp;
tormenting his older brother whenever possible.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.920
After the death of his parents, Bruce&nbsp;
Wayne swore an oath to rid Gotham City of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:12.640
its criminal underbelly. He dedicated his&nbsp;
life to training for that exact purpose.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.480
His years of training took him around the&nbsp;
world, as he worked to become an expert in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:20.960
every discipline that a master crimefighter&nbsp;
might require. Perhaps most importantly, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:26.080
trained in martial arts and as a ninja, learning&nbsp;
how to use stealth and darkness to his advantage.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:31.360
Marc Spector's superhero training came via&nbsp;
less virtuous motivations. Early in his life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.080
Marc became a boxer, despite his father's&nbsp;
insistence on a life of nonviolence. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:41.280
becoming estranged from his father, Marc enlisted&nbsp;
with the Marines, and gained some true military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.560
expertise. After that, he worked for a time as a&nbsp;
CIA agent before going his own way and becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:51.520
a mercenary for hire. Moon Knight is perfectly&nbsp;
accustomed to brutal fights and making difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:56.800
decisions when battling his enemies, because Marc&nbsp;
was doing just that long before he became a hero.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:02.960
One of Batman's defining features is his lack of&nbsp;
powers. Anyone can be Batman, provided they have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:08.320
lifetime's worth of combat and tactical training,&nbsp;
as well as billions of dollars at their disposal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:12.480
Batman may not be a regular person, but he&nbsp;
is more grounded than many of the gods and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.600
speedsters that populate DC's universe.&nbsp;
Batman uses his intelligence and gadgets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.360
to overcome the gap between himself&nbsp;
and some of his friends and foes.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.240
"What're your superpowers again?"
"I'm rich."

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:29.040
By contrast, Moon Knight actually does have&nbsp;
some special abilities in addition to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:34.480
increased physical prowess he gained from years&nbsp;
of mercenary work. His relationship with Khonshu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:40.080
gives him access to the supernatural. Sometimes he&nbsp;
receives dreams of the future from the deity; at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.960
other times, Moon Knight has increased strength,&nbsp;
depending on the phase of the moon. Despite his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:49.680
occasional burst of god-powered abilities, Moon&nbsp;
Knight tends to rely on his human strengths and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:54.240
personal training more than anything else. That&nbsp;
comes in handy for him, because Moon Knight's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.640
fractured personality sometimes leaves him&nbsp;
without the knowledge he has any powers at all.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.920
When it comes to the origins of their costumed&nbsp;
identities, Batman and Moon Knight couldn't be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:08.400
more different. Bruce Wayne trained his entire&nbsp;
life to become a crimefighter on the streets of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.280
Gotham. When he returned to the city as an adult,&nbsp;
he knew that he needed to take on a persona that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:18.400
would strike fear into the hearts of criminals.&nbsp;
Drawing on his own fear of bats as a child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.240
Bruce created the mythical figure&nbsp;
of Batman for that exact purpose.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.080
Moon Knight, on the other hand, never&nbsp;
really intended to become a superhero.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:30.880
At a young age, Marc Spector was chosen by the&nbsp;
Egyptian god of the moon, Khonshu, to become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.360
his representative on Earth. That first contact&nbsp;
with Khonshu may have been the cause of Marc's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:41.040
dissociative identity disorder, but it wasn't the&nbsp;
moment that Marc became Moon Knight. Years later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:46.080
Marc was working as a mercenary in Egypt when he&nbsp;
was betrayed and left for dead by his employer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:51.760
Bushman. Khonshu revived Marc, and conscripted&nbsp;
him as his agent on Earth. Marc returned to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:56.000
New York City and took on the identity of&nbsp;
Moon Knight to carry out Khonshu's will.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:00.800
Batman and Moon Knight have vastly different&nbsp;
relationships with their alter egos.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.240
Bruce Wayne created Batman as a symbol&nbsp;
that would allow him to fight crime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:08.720
in Gotham City more effectively than law&nbsp;
enforcement could. Over the years, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:13.280
Bruce came to identify more with his life as&nbsp;
Batman than his life as the billionaire Mr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:18.240
Wayne. Bruce's struggle to define himself within&nbsp;
two very different lives has been the subject of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:23.280
some great Batman storylines, like "Ego: A&nbsp;
Psychotic Slide into the Heart of Darkness."

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.840
If Bruce thinks he has it bad, he could really&nbsp;
use a conversation with Moon Knight. Marc Spector&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:33.040
developed dissociative identity disorder when he&nbsp;
was very young. His two primary alters are Steven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:37.680
Grant, who becomes a self-made millionaire&nbsp;
when Marc is an adult, and Jake Lockley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:43.040
who spends his time working as a cab driver. Other&nbsp;
personalities occasionally bubble to the surface,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:48.560
and sometimes Marc suffers a breakdown that causes&nbsp;
him to forget his identity entirely for a time.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.360
“Why did you call me Marc?”

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:56.160
Few superheroes' brainpower can stand up to&nbsp;
Batman's intelligence. He's earned the title&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.160 --> 00:05:00.800
"World's Greatest Detective," and it's frequently&nbsp;
Batman's careful planning and detective skills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:05.520
that help him get out of a sticky situation.&nbsp;
Batman isn't just able to think his way through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:09.920
criminal investigations, he's also more than&nbsp;
capable of designing all sorts of high-tech&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:15.280
gadgetry that aids him in his crime fighting. If&nbsp;
any Marvel superhero compares, it's Tony Stark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:19.440
who also builds his own technology and&nbsp;
tends to think his way out of problems.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:24.080
Moon Knight is by no means unintelligent, but he&nbsp;
doesn't have the same level of thoughtfulness that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:29.120
Batman so often relies on. Marc Spector has the&nbsp;
street smarts of someone who's been in and out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:34.400
every kind of combat situation imaginable. All&nbsp;
of his other personalities are equally crafty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:38.800
but none of them are going to be designing&nbsp;
futuristic tech anytime soon. That said, when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:43.520
there's a need for serious tactical know-how, Moon&nbsp;
Knight is someone that people want to have around.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:50.000
There are also very few superheroes as wealthy as&nbsp;
Batman. Wayne Enterprises is a multibillion-dollar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:54.400
company with interests in dozens of different&nbsp;
industries. Of course, Bruce Wayne inherited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:58.880
all that wealth. In fact, he has little to&nbsp;
do with the company's day-to-day operations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:02.880
but he's invested in making sure&nbsp;
Wayne Enterprises is properly managed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:07.440
After all, without the company, he'd find it&nbsp;
much harder to keep up his work as Batman.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:12.400
Marc Spector grew up in a working-class family&nbsp;
in Chicago. His mercenary days sustained him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:16.320
but Marc wasn't involved in that work for&nbsp;
the money. Once he became Moon Knight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:20.000
he was more interested in making sure&nbsp;
he had funds for equipment. Luckily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:25.280
Marc's alter Steven Grant is a capable businessman&nbsp;
who earned Moon Knight millions of dollars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:29.600
Unfortunately, due to various supernatural&nbsp;
catastrophes and mental breakdowns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:33.840
holding on to that money has never&nbsp;
been particularly easy for Moon Knight.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.440
Batman and Moon Knight have incredibly&nbsp;
different fighting styles. Batman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:41.680
prefers to attack from the shadows. He's&nbsp;
known for silently taking out enemies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:45.920
ramping up the tension and fear for everyone&nbsp;
else in the room waiting to be attacked.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:50.160
While he certainly has some weapons knowledge,&nbsp;
Batman usually fights with his fists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:54.560
and takes down bad guys with his superior&nbsp;
hand-to-hand technique and pure strength.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:58.560
Moon Knight also likes to use fear to his&nbsp;
advantage when fighting baddies, but he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:03.520
prefers to let them see him coming. Moon Knight's&nbsp;
white costume is meant to make him easily visible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:08.320
so whoever he's hunting down knows their time&nbsp;
is just about up. Due to his extensive combat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:12.960
training, Moon Knight is an expert with most&nbsp;
weapons. He can use just about anything in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:18.000
a fight, but fittingly, the Fist of Khonshu's&nbsp;
signature weapons are special crescent moon-shaped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:22.640
throwing knives. The knives are effective in&nbsp;
combat, and leave Moon Knight's mark on the scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:27.280
which helps to boost the menace of his persona&nbsp;
and instill terror into anyone he faces.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:32.480
No one stays dead in comics. Any exceptions&nbsp;
to the rule that comes to mind just haven't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:36.240
been resurrected yet. Batman and&nbsp;
Moon Knight both abide by the rule,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:40.800
but their comic-book immortality is also one&nbsp;
of their key differences. Any time that Bruce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:45.360
Wayne has "died" in the comics, there's always&nbsp;
been a secret plot twist that kept him alive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:49.120
For example, after apparently dying&nbsp;
in Final Crisis, it's revealed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:53.040
he actually became lost in time until his&nbsp;
friends were able to help bring him back.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.360
“False alarm.”
“Are you sure?”

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:00.800
Moon Knight, on the other hand, has died for real.&nbsp;
He was originally saved from death by Khonshu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:04.160
and the Egyptian god hasn't been&nbsp;
shy about resurrecting him again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:08.800
Moon Knight died for a second time in&nbsp;
issue #60, which was released in 1994&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:13.360
and ended his comic series for a time. Fans&nbsp;
might have believed his death was permanent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:19.120
but in 1997 Moon Knight returned, kicking off&nbsp;
the "Resurrection War" plot arc. Moon Knight's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:23.840
relationship with Khonshu is often strained&nbsp;
at best, so there's no guarantee the god will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:28.480
always be willing to bring the hero back from the&nbsp;
dead. However, the option is always on the table.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:34.080
The single biggest difference between Batman&nbsp;
and Moon Knight is their ideas of morality. Each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:38.880
hero's morals come from his background, and inform&nbsp;
just about every decision he makes while fighting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:43.680
crime. Young Bruce Wayne saw his parents gunned&nbsp;
down in an alley. Since then, he's been determined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:48.800
to fight evil, but he's also been committed to&nbsp;
not using guns, and not killing his enemies. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:54.000
have sometimes been exceptions to Batman's rules —&nbsp;
usually in spin-offs and alternate realities — but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:59.600
for the most part, Batman's refusal to kill is&nbsp;
the single most important aspect of his character.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:04.400
Moon Knight generally has no qualms about killing.&nbsp;
Though his father always preached nonviolence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:09.760
Moon Knight has spent his entire life embroiled in&nbsp;
one kind of fight or another. As a boxer, Marine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:14.640
and mercenary, violence was his trade. As the&nbsp;
Fist of Khonshu, Moon Knight has an obligation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:19.200
to strike down evil wherever he finds it. In&nbsp;
many ways, Moon Knight is a more vicious and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:24.320
brutal fighter than Batman, because he doesn't&nbsp;
even try to hold back his rage. Most of the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:28.320
Moon Knight is openly trying to kill his&nbsp;
opponent. Don't let white clothes fool you:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:32.400
If anything, Moon Knight is an even darker&nbsp;
character than the Dark Knight himself.

